WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:18.025
Anne stayed up all night in her room, thinking about the fact that Gilbert was dying.

2
00:00:18.026 --> 00:00:22.405
The rain beat down and the wind roared terribly outside.

3
00:00:22.406 --> 00:00:30.126
With the possibility of Gilbert gone forever, she knew now that she loved him—she had always loved him!

4
00:00:30.127 --> 00:00:36.911
If she had not been so blind . . . so foolish . . . she could be nursing him now.

5
00:00:36.912 --> 00:00:43.840
Anne sobbed. Gilbert would never know how she felt; he would die thinking that she did not care.

6
00:00:43.841 --> 00:00:50.367
Anne ached at the thought of life without Gilbert—the black years of emptiness stretching before her!

7
00:00:50.368 --> 00:00:58.504
She cowered down by her window and wished, for the first time in her happy young life, that she could die too.

8
00:00:58.505 --> 00:01:03.414
Early the next morning, she drove the buggy as fast as she could to the Blythe house.

9
00:01:03.415 --> 00:01:07.364
On the way she met one of the men who worked for Mr. Blythe.

10
00:01:07.365 --> 00:01:11.928
"Do you have any news of Gilbert Blythe?" she asked breathlessly.

11
00:01:11.929 --> 00:01:23.450
"Yes, I do," the man said. "He suddenly got much better late last night, and the doctor said he'll recover. I think he'll be all right."

12
00:01:23.451 --> 00:01:28.177
Anne turned the buggy around and drove slowly back to Green Gables.

13
00:01:28.178 --> 00:01:35.041
She could not think straight. Her head was buzzing, and she felt more alive than she had in a long time.

14
00:01:35.042 --> 00:01:41.665
This was love! For Anne it was the most beautiful morning she had ever seen.

15
00:01:41.666 --> 00:01:49.054
The birds were singing, the sun was shining brightly, and best of all, Gilbert was alive.

16
00:01:49.055 --> 00:01:53.425
After his recovery Gilbert visited Green Gables quite often.

17
00:01:53.426 --> 00:01:56.958
Anne did not mention her change in feelings to him.

18
00:01:56.959 --> 00:02:01.141
She believed that Gilbert and Christine Stuart were still a couple.

19
00:02:01.142 --> 00:02:04.306
So Anne tried her best to be just friends.

20
00:02:04.307 --> 00:02:10.364
It was difficult, though, because Anne no longer wanted friendship; she wanted Gilbert's love.

21
00:02:10.365 --> 00:02:16.347
Anne was haunted by a miserable fear that her mistake could never be fixed.

22
00:02:16.348 --> 00:02:21.493
When Gilbert came to Green Gables one afternoon, Anne was waiting for him.

23
00:02:21.494 --> 00:02:26.025
They walked to the graveyard together to put flowers on Matthew's grave.

24
00:02:26.026 --> 00:02:32.954
It was spring again, and the graveyard was particularly beautiful with all the plum trees in bloom.

25
00:02:32.955 --> 00:02:38.686
Anne gently put the flowers on Matthew's grave, and then sat under a tree with Gilbert.

26
00:02:38.687 --> 00:02:45.232
"This place is so beautiful," said Anne softly. "It's like a dream."

27
00:02:45.233 --> 00:02:48.503
"Do you have any dreams, Anne?" asked Gilbert.

28
00:02:48.504 --> 00:02:56.694
The tone of his voice sounded different, the way it had sounded that miserable evening in the orchard at Patty's Place over a year ago.

29
00:02:56.695 --> 00:03:02.900
Anne's heart beat wildly. Despite trembling inside she gave a light answer.

30
00:03:02.901 --> 00:03:07.816
"Of course, I have dreams!" she said. "Everybody has.

31
00:03:07.817 --> 00:03:12.729
We would be as good as dead if we had nothing left to dream about!"

32
00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:17.864
Gilbert turned to look at Anne. "I have a dream," he said.

33
00:03:17.865 --> 00:03:22.962
"I persist in dreaming it, although it has often seemed to me that it could never come true.

34
00:03:22.963 --> 00:03:32.555
I dream of a nice home with a fireplace in it, a cat and a dog, a big garden with fruits and vegetables, good friends coming to visit . . . and you!

35
00:03:32.556 --> 00:03:37.649
You are my dream, Anne. You always have been."

36
00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:41.629
Anne wanted to speak, but she could find no words.

37
00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:46.996
Happiness was breaking over her like a wave. It almost frightened her.

38
00:03:46.997 --> 00:03:51.020
"I asked you a question over two years ago, Anne," Gilbert said.

39
00:03:51.021 --> 00:03:54.760
"If I ask it again today, will you give me a different answer?"

40
00:03:54.761 --> 00:04:01.397
Anne still could not speak, but she lifted her head and looked steadily into Gilbert's eyes.

41
00:04:01.398 --> 00:04:08.657
She could look nowhere else. Her eyes shone with love, and Gilbert needed no other answer.

42
00:04:08.658 --> 00:04:12.828
Gilbert dared to smile, and then Anne smiled too.

43
00:04:12.829 --> 00:04:16.864
She was almost afraid to believe that what was happening was true.

44
00:04:16.865 --> 00:04:20.169
"Surely, this is a dream," she thought.

45
00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:31.398
"Gilbert, my love, my true love, telling me he loves me, on a beautiful afternoon in Avonlea . . . "

46
00:04:31.399 --> 00:04:39.232
"I thought you loved Christine Stuart," Anne later told him reproachfully, as if she had never gone out with Roy Gardner.

47
00:04:39.233 --> 00:04:44.088
Gilbert laughed. "Christine was engaged to somebody in her hometown.

48
00:04:44.089 --> 00:04:48.407
I knew it, and she knew that I knew it. I was friends with her brother.

49
00:04:48.408 --> 00:04:54.975
He told me his sister was coming to Halifax, and asked me if I would look after her. So I did."

50
00:04:54.976 --> 00:04:59.560
Gilbert continued, "Christine is one of the nicest girls I've ever known.

51
00:04:59.561 --> 00:05:03.349
I knew college gossip said we were in love, but I didn't care.

52
00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:08.142
After you told me you could never love me, Anne, nothing mattered much to me for a while.

53
00:05:08.143 --> 00:05:13.109
There was nobody else. There never could be anybody but you for me.

54
00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:17.708
I've loved you ever since that day you broke your slate over my head in school."

55
00:05:17.709 --> 00:05:23.556
"I don't see how you could keep on loving me when I was such a little fool," said Anne.

56
00:05:23.557 --> 00:05:33.261
"Well, I tried to stop," said Gilbert honestly, "and it wasn't easy being told every week by some busybody that you were almost engaged!

57
00:05:33.262 --> 00:05:36.152
Things only changed a few weeks ago.

58
00:05:36.153 --> 00:05:41.696
I had been really sick—close to dying, the doctor said—when a letter arrived from Phil Gordon.

59
00:05:41.697 --> 00:05:45.885
She told me that there was nothing between you and Roy, and that I should try again.

60
00:05:45.886 --> 00:05:52.559
Well, the doctor was amazed at my rapid recovery after that." Gilbert smiled lovingly at Anne.

61
00:05:52.560 --> 00:06:00.012
Anne laughed and then shivered. "I can never forget the night I thought you were dying, Gilbert.

62
00:06:00.013 --> 00:06:07.585
Oh, I knew . . . I knew then how much I loved you . . . and I feared it was too late."

63
00:06:07.586 --> 00:06:13.933
"But it wasn't, Anne, my love," Gilbert said, and he drew Anne close to him and kissed her.

64
00:06:13.934 --> 00:06:25.441
They walked home together in the dusk, happy and together in love.
